WEBVTT

00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:08.223
Dad. Sam.

00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:09.857
This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:11.824
Sam: if this demon killed mom
and jess and dad's closing in,

00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:13.024
We got to help.

00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:14.590
Dad doesn't want our help.

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:17.957
I'm talking one week here, man,
to get answers, to get revenge.

00:00:17.991 --> 00:00:19.223
You think i didn't respect dad.

00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:20.891
Sorry i brought it up. I respected him.

00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:22.891
No matter what i did,
it was never good enough.

00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:24.590
So what are you saying? That
dad was disappointed in you?

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.257
When we finally do find dad,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.091
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:30.924
Hey! Dad.

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:32.091
Hey, boys.

00:00:32.124 --> 00:00:34.290
Hi, sam. Hi, dad.

00:00:34.323 --> 00:00:36.924
Last time we were together,
we had one hell of a fight.

00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:39.424
Yes, sir. It's good to see you again.

00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.357
It's been a long time.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.390
Sam!

00:00:42.424 --> 00:00:43.724
Dean: we almost got dad killed.

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:45.290
They're not gonna stop.
They're gonna try again.

00:00:45.323 --> 00:00:47.024
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:00:47.058 --> 00:00:48.791
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:50.290
I got to be a part of this fight.

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:51.924
Sammy, this fight is just starting.

00:00:51.957 --> 00:00:54.024
You got to let me go.

00:01:14.357 --> 00:01:15.891
Beth: mr. Elkins?

00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:19.624
Mr. Elkins.

00:01:19.657 --> 00:01:21.724
Would you like another?

00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:24.390
Yeah. Thanks, beth.

00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:29.657
I thought they caught the unabomber.

00:01:29.691 --> 00:01:32.891
Yeah, poor mr. Elkins lives
all alone up in the canyon.

00:01:32.924 --> 00:01:35.657
Same seat every day,

00:01:35.691 --> 00:01:37.957
Going through his papers,
making his little notes.

00:01:37.991 --> 00:01:41.257
He's a nice old man. He's just a nut.

00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:45.457
Here you go.

00:02:11.091 --> 00:02:12.357
What'll you have?

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.824
Jack all around. Leave the bottle.

00:02:14.857 --> 00:02:17.490
You hungry? We have dinner plans.

00:02:21.691 --> 00:02:24.158
Can i get you something
else, mr. Elkins?

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:13.991
It's been a while.

00:03:14.024 --> 00:03:16.091
I got to say, you look old.

00:03:16.124 --> 00:03:18.424
What do you want? What do you think?

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.924
Damn.

00:03:26.457 --> 00:03:27.724
You can do better than that.

00:03:38.991 --> 00:03:40.524
Come on, come on.

00:04:22.757 --> 00:04:24.091
Nice gun.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.857
Wouldn't do you much good, of course.

00:04:28.891 --> 00:04:31.390
Boys...

00:04:31.424 --> 00:04:33.824
We're eating in tonight.

00:04:54.091 --> 00:04:56.657
All right, dude, not a decent
lead in all of nebraska.

00:04:56.691 --> 00:04:57.891
What do you got?

00:04:57.924 --> 00:05:00.857
Well, i been scanning wyoming,
colorado, south dakota.

00:05:00.891 --> 00:05:03.991
Here
- A woman in iowa fell 10,000 feet from an airplane

00:05:04.024 --> 00:05:05.757
And survived.

00:05:05.791 --> 00:05:07.557
Sounds more like "that's incredible!"

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.158
Than "the twilight zone."

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.390
Yeah.

00:05:10.424 --> 00:05:13.323
Hey, you know, we could
just keep heading east -

00:05:13.357 --> 00:05:15.557
New york, upstate.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.924
Could stop by and see sarah again. Huh?

00:05:17.957 --> 00:05:20.524
She's a cool chick, man. Smokin'.

00:05:20.557 --> 00:05:24.058
You two seemed pretty
friendly. What do you say?

00:05:24.091 --> 00:05:26.058
Yeah, i don't know. Maybe someday.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.824
But in the meantime, we got
a lot of work to do, dean,

00:05:28.857 --> 00:05:30.058
And you know that.

00:05:30.091 --> 00:05:31.757
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:33.991
What else you got?

00:05:34.024 --> 00:05:35.257
Uh, man in colorado.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.624
Local man by the name of daniel elkins

00:05:37.657 --> 00:05:39.524
Was found mauled in his home.

00:05:39.557 --> 00:05:42.091
Elkins. I know that name.

00:05:42.124 --> 00:05:44.091
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:44.124 --> 00:05:46.124
Looks like the cops
don't know what to think.

00:05:46.158 --> 00:05:49.490
At first they said it was
some sort of bear attack,

00:05:49.524 --> 00:05:51.824
And now they found signs of robbery.

00:05:51.857 --> 00:05:53.223
Mm-Hmm.

00:05:53.257 --> 00:05:55.424
Yeah.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.891
Here. Check it out.

00:06:06.724 --> 00:06:08.557
You think it's the same elkins?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.891
It's a colorado area code.

00:06:48.924 --> 00:06:51.490
Looks like the maid didn't come today.

00:06:57.257 --> 00:06:59.724
Hey, there's salt over
here, right inside the door.

00:06:59.757 --> 00:07:01.991
You mean, like,
protection-Against-Demon salt

00:07:02.024 --> 00:07:03.957
Or "oops, i spilled the popcorn" salt?

00:07:03.991 --> 00:07:05.691
It's clearly a ring.

00:07:10.158 --> 00:07:13.357
You think this guy elkins was a player?

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.457
Definitely.

00:07:23.924 --> 00:07:26.390
That looks a hell of a lot like dad's.

00:07:26.424 --> 00:07:29.857
Except this dates back to the '60s.

00:07:54.791 --> 00:07:57.924
Whatever attacked him, looks
like there was more than one.

00:07:57.957 --> 00:08:00.557
Looks like he put up
a hell of a fight, too.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.957
Yeah.

00:08:29.357 --> 00:08:31.590
Got something?

00:08:33.257 --> 00:08:36.257
I don't know. Some
scratches in the floor.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.590
Death throes maybe?

00:08:37.624 --> 00:08:39.457
Maybe.

00:08:58.624 --> 00:09:00.357
Or maybe a message.

00:09:03.124 --> 00:09:06.490
Look familiar?

00:09:06.524 --> 00:09:08.757
Three letters, six digits -

00:09:08.791 --> 00:09:12.791
The location and combination
of a post office box.

00:09:12.824 --> 00:09:14.124
It's a mail drop.

00:09:14.158 --> 00:09:16.091
That's just the way dad does it.

00:09:34.891 --> 00:09:39.024
"J.W."
- You think? John winchester?

00:09:39.058 --> 00:09:41.058
I don't know. Should we open it?

00:09:45.223 --> 00:09:47.058
Dad?

00:09:49.624 --> 00:09:51.924
Dad, what are you doing
here? Are you all right?

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:52.991
Yeah, i'm okay.

00:09:53.024 --> 00:09:54.524
Look, i read the news about daniel.

00:09:54.557 --> 00:09:57.158
I got here as fast as i could.

00:09:58.924 --> 00:10:01.357
I saw you two up at his place.

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.158
Why didn't you come in, dad?

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.457
You know why.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.190
Because i had to make sure
you weren't followed...

00:10:07.223 --> 00:10:08.991
By anyone...

00:10:09.024 --> 00:10:10.691
Or anything.

00:10:10.724 --> 00:10:14.058
Nice job of covering
your tracks, by the way.

00:10:14.091 --> 00:10:16.957
Yeah, well, we learned from the best.

00:10:16.991 --> 00:10:19.957
Wait, so you came all the way
out here for this elkins guy?

00:10:19.991 --> 00:10:21.158
Yeah.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:25.058
He was
- He was a good man.

00:10:25.091 --> 00:10:27.524
He taught me a hell
of a lot about hunting.

00:10:27.557 --> 00:10:31.024
You never mentioned him to us.

00:10:31.058 --> 00:10:33.590
We had a -

00:10:33.624 --> 00:10:36.257
We had kind of a falling out.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.924
I hadn't seen him in years.

00:10:40.791 --> 00:10:42.991
I should look at that.

00:10:51.524 --> 00:10:55.590
"If you're reading
this, i'm already dead."

00:10:55.624 --> 00:10:57.891
That son of a bitch. What is it?

00:10:57.924 --> 00:11:00.223
He had it the whole time. Dad, what?

00:11:00.257 --> 00:11:01.757
When you searched the place,

00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:04.190
Did you see a gun, an
antique, a colt revolver?

00:11:04.223 --> 00:11:05.323
Did you see it?

00:11:05.357 --> 00:11:07.557
Uh, there was an old
case, but it was empty.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:09.490
They have it. You mean
whatever killed elkins?

00:11:09.524 --> 00:11:11.390
We got to pick up their trail.

00:11:12.924 --> 00:11:15.891
Wait. You want us to come with you?

00:11:15.924 --> 00:11:18.257
If elkins is telling the truth,
we've got to find this gun.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.757
The gun? Why? Because
it's important, that's why.

00:11:20.791 --> 00:11:23.058
Dad, we don't even know
what these things are yet.

00:11:23.091 --> 00:11:25.091
They were what danny
elkins killed best...

00:11:25.124 --> 00:11:27.257
Vampires.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.290
Vampires?

00:11:28.323 --> 00:11:30.190
I thought there was no such thing.

00:11:30.223 --> 00:11:32.457
You never even mentioned them, dad.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.857
I thought they were extinct.

00:11:34.891 --> 00:11:38.924
I thought elkins and
others had wiped them out.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:43.657
I was wrong.

00:11:45.657 --> 00:11:49.024
John: most vampire lore is
crap. A cross won't repel them.

00:11:49.058 --> 00:11:50.490
Sunlight won't kill them

00:11:50.524 --> 00:11:52.857
And neither will a stake to the heart.

00:11:52.891 --> 00:11:55.124
But the bloodlust
- That part's true.

00:11:55.158 --> 00:11:57.457
They need fresh human blood to survive.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.891
They were once people,

00:11:58.924 --> 00:12:02.158
So you won't know it's a
vampire until it's too late.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.924
All yours, baby.

00:12:10.257 --> 00:12:12.390
What?

00:12:12.424 --> 00:12:14.190
Well, i guess you showed that guy.

00:12:14.223 --> 00:12:16.991
What guy? The guy who bet you
you wouldn't buy that shirt.

00:12:17.024 --> 00:12:19.223
I love this shirt.

00:12:21.891 --> 00:12:23.323
Look out!

00:12:27.691 --> 00:12:29.390
What happened to him?

00:12:29.424 --> 00:12:31.190
Call 911.

00:12:54.954 --> 00:12:57.520
Man: 22, i'm going out there.

00:12:57.554 --> 00:12:59.354
Man #2: copy that.

00:13:04.821 --> 00:13:08.153
Sam, dean, let's go.

00:13:08.187 --> 00:13:09.487
Picked up a police call.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.687
What happened?

00:13:10.721 --> 00:13:13.187
A couple called 911. They
found a body in the street.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.021
Cops got there. Everyone was missing.

00:13:15.054 --> 00:13:16.253
It's the vampires.

00:13:16.287 --> 00:13:17.687
How do you know?

00:13:17.721 --> 00:13:19.554
Just follow me, okay?

00:13:21.954 --> 00:13:23.687
Vampires.

00:13:23.721 --> 00:13:26.021
It's funny every time i hear it.

00:13:26.054 --> 00:13:28.220
[ Indistinct chatter on police radio ]

00:13:32.187 --> 00:13:34.587
I don't see why we couldn't
have gone over with him.

00:13:34.621 --> 00:13:36.554
Oh, don't tell me it's already starting.

00:13:36.587 --> 00:13:38.687
What's starting?

00:13:38.721 --> 00:13:40.454
What do you got? It was them all right.

00:13:40.487 --> 00:13:42.088
It looks like they're heading west.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.220
We have to double back
to get around that detour.

00:13:44.253 --> 00:13:45.621
How can you be so sure?

00:13:45.654 --> 00:13:47.587
I just want to know we're
going in the right direction.

00:13:47.621 --> 00:13:49.253
We are.

00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:51.187
How do you know?

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.253
I found this.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.554
What is it? A vampire fang?

00:13:58.587 --> 00:14:01.721
No fangs
- Teeth. The second set descends when they attack.

00:14:01.754 --> 00:14:03.420
Any more questions?

00:14:06.654 --> 00:14:08.921
Let's get out of here.
We're losing daylight.

00:14:08.954 --> 00:14:12.721
And, dean, why don't you touch
up your car before you get rust?

00:14:12.754 --> 00:14:14.621
I wouldn't have given you the damn thing

00:14:14.654 --> 00:14:17.253
If i thought you were gonna ruin it.

00:14:24.487 --> 00:14:26.487
Vampires nest in groups of 8 to 10.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.921
Smaller packs are sent
out to hunt for food.

00:14:28.954 --> 00:14:32.187
Victims are taken to the nest,
where the pack keeps them alive,

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.088
Bleeding them for days or weeks.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:36.787
I wonder if that's what
happened to that 911 couple.

00:14:36.821 --> 00:14:38.787
That's probably what dad's thinking.

00:14:38.821 --> 00:14:43.420
Of course, it would be nice if
he just told us what he thinks.

00:14:43.454 --> 00:14:45.287
<i>So it is starting.</i>

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.021
What?

00:14:48.054 --> 00:14:49.921
Sam, we've been looking
for dad all year.

00:14:49.954 --> 00:14:52.287
Now we're not with him for
more than a couple of hours

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.487
And there's static already.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:56.253
No.

00:14:56.287 --> 00:14:58.520
Look, i'm happy he's okay, all right,

00:14:58.554 --> 00:15:00.420
And i'm happy that we're
all working together.

00:15:00.454 --> 00:15:02.320
Good.

00:15:02.354 --> 00:15:06.520
It's just the way he treats
us like we're children.

00:15:06.554 --> 00:15:07.988
He barks orders at us, dean.

00:15:08.021 --> 00:15:10.354
He expects us to follow
him without question.

00:15:10.387 --> 00:15:12.687
He keeps us on some
crap need-To-Know deal.

00:15:12.721 --> 00:15:14.654
He does what he does for
a reason. What reason?

00:15:14.687 --> 00:15:15.887
Our job!

00:15:15.921 --> 00:15:17.721
There's no time to argue.
There's no margin for error.

00:15:17.754 --> 00:15:19.220
It's just the way the
old man runs things.

00:15:19.253 --> 00:15:21.120
Yeah, well, maybe that
worked when we were kids,

00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:22.487
But not anymore, all right?

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.721
Not after everything you and
i have been through, dean.

00:15:24.754 --> 00:15:27.187
Are you telling me you're cool
with just falling into line

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:28.854
And letting him run the whole show?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:34.088
If that's what it takes.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.320
Have some beer, buddy.

00:16:00.354 --> 00:16:02.554
It'll calm your nerves.

00:16:02.587 --> 00:16:04.021
No, thanks.

00:16:04.054 --> 00:16:05.320
Oh, come on.

00:16:05.354 --> 00:16:07.787
You drink enough, i can
taste it in your blood.

00:16:07.821 --> 00:16:09.520
That's gross.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.021
Well, how about you, babe?

00:16:27.287 --> 00:16:28.520
Attagirl.

00:16:35.153 --> 00:16:37.387
Bo! Wait for luther.

00:16:59.487 --> 00:17:02.220
I missed you, too, baby.

00:17:02.253 --> 00:17:04.854
We've got presents.

00:17:11.287 --> 00:17:12.721
She looks interesting.

00:17:14.787 --> 00:17:15.787
Hmm.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:19.654
He doesn't.

00:17:19.687 --> 00:17:21.021
Lock him up.

00:17:23.887 --> 00:17:26.921
On second thought, go
ahead and treat yourself.

00:17:31.988 --> 00:17:35.487
[ Crying ] no!

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.054
There's something else.

00:17:39.021 --> 00:17:40.454
This all theirs?

00:17:40.487 --> 00:17:43.854
No. It's from an old friend of yours...

00:17:43.887 --> 00:17:45.387
Daniel elkins.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.354
I caught his scent.

00:17:47.387 --> 00:17:49.887
I thought i'd surprise you.

00:17:49.921 --> 00:17:51.787
Kate, what did you do?

00:17:51.821 --> 00:17:53.520
I made him suffer.

00:17:53.554 --> 00:17:55.621
You shouldn't have done that.

00:17:55.654 --> 00:17:57.021
There are others like him.

00:17:57.054 --> 00:17:59.054
They'll know the signs
and come looking for us.

00:17:59.088 --> 00:18:00.153
We have to be careful.

00:18:00.187 --> 00:18:01.454
Luther, i did it for you,

00:18:01.487 --> 00:18:02.988
For what he did to your family.

00:18:03.021 --> 00:18:05.021
Revenge isn't worth
much if you end up dead.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.887
I'm sorry, babe.

00:18:09.921 --> 00:18:12.253
I'm sorry.

00:18:18.153 --> 00:18:20.153
I thought you might like that.

00:18:20.187 --> 00:18:22.921
Looks like it was made
around the time you were born.

00:18:24.954 --> 00:18:26.821
I've seen this before.

00:18:26.854 --> 00:18:29.387
Elkins died with it in his hands.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:33.320
He should have known better
- Using a gun.

00:18:33.354 --> 00:18:36.721
This is no ordinary gun.

00:18:36.754 --> 00:18:38.887
Yeah, dad. All right, got it.

00:18:38.921 --> 00:18:40.988
Pull off the next exit. Why?

00:18:41.021 --> 00:18:43.054
'Cause dad thinks we
got the vampires' trail.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:44.120
How?

00:18:44.153 --> 00:18:46.354
I don't know. He didn't say.

00:18:57.854 --> 00:19:00.420
Oh, crap. Here we go.

00:19:00.454 --> 00:19:02.287
What the hell was that? We need to talk.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.754
About what? About everything.

00:19:03.787 --> 00:19:06.287
Where we going, dad? What's
the big deal about this gun?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.387
We can q&a after we
kill all the vampires.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.654
Your brother's right. We
don't have time for this.

00:19:10.687 --> 00:19:13.054
Last we saw you, you said it
was too dangerous to be together.

00:19:13.088 --> 00:19:14.687
Now, out of the blue, you need our help.

00:19:14.721 --> 00:19:17.120
Obviously something big's going
down, and we want to know what!

00:19:17.153 --> 00:19:19.253
Get back in the car. No.

00:19:19.287 --> 00:19:21.520
I said get back in the damn car.

00:19:21.554 --> 00:19:22.921
Yeah, and i said no.

00:19:22.954 --> 00:19:24.621
All right, you made
your point, tough guy.

00:19:24.654 --> 00:19:26.887
Look, we're all tired. We
can talk about this later.

00:19:26.921 --> 00:19:28.187
Sammy, i mean it. Come on.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.854
This is why i left in the first place.

00:19:29.887 --> 00:19:31.754
What'd you say? You heard me.

00:19:31.787 --> 00:19:32.821
<i>Yeah, you left.</i>

00:19:32.854 --> 00:19:35.287
Your brother and me
- We needed you.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.854
You walked away, sam. You walked away!

00:19:37.887 --> 00:19:40.320
You're the one who said,
"don't come back," dad.

00:19:40.354 --> 00:19:42.621
You're the one who
closed that door, not me!

00:19:42.654 --> 00:19:45.420
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:19:45.454 --> 00:19:47.153
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:19:47.187 --> 00:19:49.187
That's enough!

00:19:50.687 --> 00:19:52.287
That means you, too.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:01.687
Terrific.

00:20:24.954 --> 00:20:27.021
Luther: you like to watch, huh?

00:20:27.054 --> 00:20:29.220
Me too.

00:20:31.487 --> 00:20:33.153
Ready, baby?

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:50.721
Are you gonna kill me?

00:20:50.754 --> 00:20:55.187
I'm gonna take you so high
you're never gonna come down.

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.487
Welcome home, baby.

00:21:52.827 --> 00:21:54.427
I know what time it is.

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:55.927
Get in.

00:21:59.261 --> 00:22:02.328
Dean: son of a bitch.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:04.827
So they're really not afraid of the sun?

00:22:04.861 --> 00:22:07.694
No, direct sunlight hurts
like a nasty sunburn.

00:22:07.727 --> 00:22:11.594
The only way to kill
them is by beheading.

00:22:11.627 --> 00:22:15.061
And, yeah, they sleep during the day.

00:22:15.094 --> 00:22:18.493
It doesn't mean they won't wake up.

00:22:18.527 --> 00:22:21.994
So i guess walking right
in's not our best option.

00:22:22.027 --> 00:22:24.894
Actually, that's the plan.

00:22:32.927 --> 00:22:34.527
Dad, i've got an extra
machete if you need one.

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:38.061
Think i'm okay. Thanks.

00:22:38.094 --> 00:22:40.027
Wow.

00:22:46.694 --> 00:22:49.460
So...

00:22:49.493 --> 00:22:52.161
You boys really want
to know about this colt?

00:22:56.261 --> 00:22:57.794
Yes, sir.

00:22:57.827 --> 00:23:00.261
It's just a story...

00:23:00.294 --> 00:23:03.261
A legend, really.

00:23:03.294 --> 00:23:05.393
Well, i thought it was.

00:23:05.427 --> 00:23:08.393
Never really believed it
until i read daniel's letter.

00:23:08.427 --> 00:23:12.294
Back in 1835, when
halley's comet was overhead,

00:23:12.328 --> 00:23:15.927
The same night those
men died at the alamo,

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:18.861
They say samuel colt made a gun...

00:23:18.894 --> 00:23:20.161
A special gun.

00:23:20.194 --> 00:23:22.261
He made it for a hunter -

00:23:22.294 --> 00:23:25.660
A man like us, only on horseback.

00:23:25.694 --> 00:23:28.627
The story goes he made 13 bullets.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:32.594
This hunter used the
gun a half dozen times

00:23:32.627 --> 00:23:36.927
Before he disappeared,
the gun along with him.

00:23:36.961 --> 00:23:40.427
Somehow, daniel got his hands on it.

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:42.760
They say -

00:23:42.794 --> 00:23:45.427
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:48.894
Kill anything, like
supernatural anything?

00:23:50.127 --> 00:23:51.894
Like the demon.

00:23:51.927 --> 00:23:53.760
Yeah, the demon.

00:23:53.794 --> 00:23:56.660
Ever since i picked up its trail,

00:23:56.694 --> 00:24:00.861
I've been looking for a
way to destroy that thing.

00:24:00.894 --> 00:24:04.794
Find the gun...

00:24:04.827 --> 00:24:07.328
We may have it.

00:25:38.994 --> 00:25:40.927
Sam: dean.

00:26:04.861 --> 00:26:06.660
There's more.

00:26:41.627 --> 00:26:44.161
Hey.

00:26:44.194 --> 00:26:46.261
Hey, hey, shh. I'm here to help you.

00:26:58.827 --> 00:27:00.493
John: boys, run!

00:27:01.393 --> 00:27:02.594
Dad!

00:27:10.861 --> 00:27:12.427
Dad?!

00:27:14.760 --> 00:27:16.493
Dad?!

00:27:21.727 --> 00:27:24.027
They won't follow. They'll till tonight.

00:27:24.061 --> 00:27:26.460
Once a vampire gets your
scent, it's for life.

00:27:26.493 --> 00:27:27.694
What do we do now?

00:27:27.727 --> 00:27:29.794
You got to find the
nearest funeral home.

00:27:32.560 --> 00:27:34.961
It shouldn't be taking this long.

00:27:34.994 --> 00:27:37.427
I should go help.

00:27:37.460 --> 00:27:39.827
Dean's got it.

00:27:47.360 --> 00:27:49.194
Sammy.

00:27:50.861 --> 00:27:51.861
Yeah?

00:27:54.794 --> 00:27:57.328
I don't think i ever told you this,

00:27:57.360 --> 00:28:00.594
But the day you were
born, you know what i did?

00:28:00.627 --> 00:28:02.694
No.

00:28:02.727 --> 00:28:05.794
I put 100 bucks into a
savings account for you.

00:28:05.827 --> 00:28:08.427
I did the same thing for your brother.

00:28:11.194 --> 00:28:12.727
It was a college fund.

00:28:15.061 --> 00:28:20.228
And every month, i'd put
in another $100 until...

00:28:22.261 --> 00:28:24.660
Anyway, my point is, sam, that

00:28:26.660 --> 00:28:28.794
This is never the life
that i wanted for you.

00:28:28.827 --> 00:28:31.527
Then why'd you get so mad when i left?

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:35.061
You got to understand something.

00:28:35.094 --> 00:28:37.660
After your mother passed,

00:28:37.694 --> 00:28:41.527
All i saw was evil, everywhere.

00:28:41.560 --> 00:28:47.094
And all i cared about was
keeping you boys alive.

00:28:47.127 --> 00:28:50.594
I wanted you prepared...

00:28:50.627 --> 00:28:52.127
Ready.

00:28:54.360 --> 00:28:56.961
So somewhere along the line, i, uh

00:28:59.660 --> 00:29:01.660
I stopped being your father.

00:29:01.694 --> 00:29:03.560
And i -

00:29:03.594 --> 00:29:07.261
I became your drill sergeant.

00:29:09.294 --> 00:29:13.094
So when you said you
wanted to go away to school,

00:29:13.127 --> 00:29:16.393
All i could think
about, my only thought,

00:29:16.427 --> 00:29:21.460
Was that you were gonna be alone...

00:29:21.493 --> 00:29:23.427
Vulnerable.

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:26.261
Sammy, it just -

00:29:26.294 --> 00:29:28.427
It never occurred to me what you wanted.

00:29:30.294 --> 00:29:32.594
I just couldn't accept the fact

00:29:32.627 --> 00:29:35.393
That you and me...

00:29:35.427 --> 00:29:36.594
We're just different.

00:29:38.194 --> 00:29:39.460
What?

00:29:42.727 --> 00:29:44.294
We're not different.

00:29:46.727 --> 00:29:48.861
Not anymore.

00:29:51.660 --> 00:29:54.360
With what happened to mom and jess

00:29:58.127 --> 00:30:00.194
We probably have a lot more in common

00:30:00.228 --> 00:30:02.927
Than just about anyone.

00:30:05.294 --> 00:30:07.660
I guess you're right, son.

00:30:11.393 --> 00:30:13.560
Hey, dad?

00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.760
Whatever happened to that college fund?

00:30:19.727 --> 00:30:21.527
Spent it on ammo.

00:30:28.594 --> 00:30:29.961
Whoo!

00:30:29.994 --> 00:30:33.493
Man, there's some heavy security
to protect a bunch of dead guys.

00:30:33.527 --> 00:30:35.694
Did you get it?

00:30:45.161 --> 00:30:48.061
You know what to do.

00:30:56.961 --> 00:30:58.627
Kate: car trouble?

00:31:02.794 --> 00:31:04.994
Let me give you a lift...

00:31:05.027 --> 00:31:06.927
Take you back to my place.

00:31:06.961 --> 00:31:08.061
I'll pass.

00:31:08.094 --> 00:31:10.427
I usually draw the line at necrophilia.

00:31:24.727 --> 00:31:28.360
I don't normally get this
friendly till the second date.

00:31:28.393 --> 00:31:31.427
You know, we could have some fun.

00:31:31.460 --> 00:31:34.627
I always like to make new friends.

00:31:44.527 --> 00:31:47.393
Oh, sorry.

00:31:47.427 --> 00:31:49.827
I never really stay
with a chick that long.

00:31:49.861 --> 00:31:51.161
Definitely not eternity.

00:31:51.194 --> 00:31:52.427
Ugh!

00:31:56.861 --> 00:31:58.861
Damn it.

00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:02.194
Barely even stings.

00:32:02.228 --> 00:32:04.560
Give it time, sweetheart.

00:32:04.594 --> 00:32:06.827
That arrow's soaked in dead man's blood.

00:32:06.861 --> 00:32:09.294
It's like poison to you, isn't it?

00:32:12.560 --> 00:32:13.861
Load her up.

00:32:13.894 --> 00:32:16.294
I'll take care of this one.

00:32:26.951 --> 00:32:28.250
Toss this on the fire.

00:32:28.284 --> 00:32:30.384
Saffron, skunks,
cabbage, and trillium -

00:32:30.417 --> 00:32:32.984
It'll block our scent and
hers until we're ready.

00:32:33.018 --> 00:32:34.817
Stuff stinks. Well, that's the idea.

00:32:34.851 --> 00:32:36.517
Dust your clothes with the ashes

00:32:36.551 --> 00:32:38.817
And you'll stand a chance
of not being detected.

00:32:38.851 --> 00:32:40.484
You sure they'll come after her?

00:32:40.517 --> 00:32:42.651
Yeah. Vampires mate for life.

00:32:42.684 --> 00:32:45.150
She means more to the
leader than the gun.

00:32:45.183 --> 00:32:47.117
But the blood sickness
is gonna wear off soon,

00:32:47.150 --> 00:32:48.584
So you don't have a lot of time.

00:32:48.617 --> 00:32:50.083
Half-Hour ought to do it.

00:32:50.117 --> 00:32:52.884
And then i want you out of
the area as fast as you can.

00:32:52.918 --> 00:32:54.117
But -

00:32:54.150 --> 00:32:55.717
You can't take care
of them all yourself.

00:32:55.751 --> 00:32:58.083
I'll have her and the colt.

00:32:58.117 --> 00:33:01.617
But after, we're gonna meet up, right?

00:33:01.651 --> 00:33:05.250
Use the gun together, right?

00:33:07.150 --> 00:33:09.517
You're leaving again, aren't you?

00:33:11.684 --> 00:33:15.150
You still want to go
after the demon alone?

00:33:15.183 --> 00:33:16.651
You know, i don't get you.

00:33:16.684 --> 00:33:19.250
You can't treat us like this. Like what?

00:33:19.284 --> 00:33:20.450
Like children.

00:33:20.484 --> 00:33:23.617
You are my children. I'm
trying to keep you safe.

00:33:23.651 --> 00:33:26.450
Dad, all due respect, but
that's a bunch of crap.

00:33:27.384 --> 00:33:29.517
Excuse me?

00:33:29.551 --> 00:33:31.584
You know what sammy
and i have been hunting.

00:33:31.617 --> 00:33:33.884
Hell, you sent us on a
few hunting trips yourself.

00:33:33.918 --> 00:33:36.050
You can't be that worried
about keeping us safe.

00:33:36.083 --> 00:33:37.617
It's not the same thing, de.

00:33:37.651 --> 00:33:38.751
Then what is it?

00:33:38.784 --> 00:33:40.817
Why do you want us out of the big fight?

00:33:40.851 --> 00:33:42.684
This demon...

00:33:42.717 --> 00:33:45.851
It's a bad son of a bitch.

00:33:45.884 --> 00:33:47.417
I can't make the same moves

00:33:47.450 --> 00:33:49.751
If i'm worried about keeping you alive.

00:33:49.784 --> 00:33:50.951
You can't be as reckless.

00:33:50.984 --> 00:33:52.384
Look...

00:33:52.417 --> 00:33:55.984
I don't expect to make it out
of this fight in one piece.

00:33:58.183 --> 00:34:01.617
Your mother's death...

00:34:01.651 --> 00:34:03.250
It almost killed me.

00:34:04.884 --> 00:34:08.751
I can't watch my children die, too.

00:34:08.784 --> 00:34:09.918
I won't.

00:34:09.951 --> 00:34:11.984
What happens if you die?

00:34:12.018 --> 00:34:13.984
Dad, what happens if you die

00:34:14.018 --> 00:34:16.484
And we could have done
something about it?

00:34:16.517 --> 00:34:17.751
You know, i've been thinking.

00:34:17.784 --> 00:34:19.651
I think maybe sammy's
right about this one.

00:34:19.684 --> 00:34:21.317
I think we should do this together.

00:34:23.584 --> 00:34:26.183
We're stronger as a family,
dad. We just are. You know it.

00:34:27.651 --> 00:34:29.250
We're running out of time.

00:34:30.684 --> 00:34:33.350
You do your job, and
you get out of the area.

00:34:34.584 --> 00:34:36.517
That's an order.

00:34:46.484 --> 00:34:48.684
Is there any sign of those three?

00:34:48.717 --> 00:34:50.651
No. Something else.

00:34:50.684 --> 00:34:52.751
What? Luther, they cut off hank's head.

00:34:52.784 --> 00:34:54.851
And kate?

00:34:54.884 --> 00:34:57.884
I don't know. She wasn't there.

00:34:59.350 --> 00:35:01.018
What are we gonna do?

00:35:06.317 --> 00:35:08.884
It's just a truck up on the highway.

00:35:13.984 --> 00:35:16.417
Kate.

00:35:16.450 --> 00:35:18.717
She's in that truck.

00:36:18.851 --> 00:36:20.284
Boo.

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:38.684
I told you i'd come back.

00:36:57.450 --> 00:36:59.551
Luther: get out!

00:37:03.784 --> 00:37:05.018
Who are you?

00:37:05.050 --> 00:37:06.384
The name's winchester.

00:37:06.417 --> 00:37:07.851
Where are your friends?

00:37:07.884 --> 00:37:09.450
Cleaning out your nest.

00:37:11.784 --> 00:37:13.484
Where's kate?

00:37:13.517 --> 00:37:15.651
Come here, sweetheart.

00:37:23.250 --> 00:37:25.183
Kate, you all right?

00:37:27.083 --> 00:37:29.317
Dead man's blood.

00:37:29.350 --> 00:37:31.384
You son of a bitch.

00:37:31.417 --> 00:37:35.083
I want the colt
- Elkins' gun.

00:37:35.117 --> 00:37:36.117
Trade.

00:37:36.150 --> 00:37:37.517
Is that what this is all about?

00:37:37.551 --> 00:37:39.350
I mean, you can't shoot us all, right?

00:37:39.384 --> 00:37:40.817
We'll kill you.

00:37:40.851 --> 00:37:43.484
Oh, i don't need it for you.

00:37:43.517 --> 00:37:46.484
I'm saving it for something else.

00:37:46.517 --> 00:37:50.083
Now, put the colt
down or she goes first.

00:37:50.117 --> 00:37:52.717
All right.

00:37:52.751 --> 00:37:55.018
Just don't hurt her.

00:38:02.350 --> 00:38:03.617
Back up.

00:38:05.784 --> 00:38:07.150
Further.

00:38:19.050 --> 00:38:21.551
That's a nice move. You almost made it.

00:38:46.150 --> 00:38:47.183
Ugh!

00:38:51.651 --> 00:38:54.150
Don't! I'll break his neck.

00:38:54.183 --> 00:38:55.851
Put the blade down.

00:39:09.117 --> 00:39:11.717
You people.

00:39:11.751 --> 00:39:13.751
Why can't you just leave us alone?

00:39:13.784 --> 00:39:16.083
We have as much right to live as you do.

00:39:16.117 --> 00:39:17.651
John: i don't think so.

00:39:44.217 --> 00:39:46.884
Luther!

00:40:02.018 --> 00:40:04.117
Kate, don't!

00:40:27.984 --> 00:40:29.984
So, boys...

00:40:34.283 --> 00:40:35.951
Yes, sir?

00:40:35.984 --> 00:40:38.517
You ignored a direct order back there.

00:40:38.550 --> 00:40:40.917
Yes, sir. But we saved your ass.

00:40:46.218 --> 00:40:47.617
You're right.

00:40:47.650 --> 00:40:49.951
I am?

00:40:49.984 --> 00:40:52.350
It scares the hell out of me.

00:40:52.383 --> 00:40:54.250
You two are all i've got.

00:40:56.151 --> 00:40:59.884
But i guess we are stronger as a family.

00:40:59.917 --> 00:41:02.584
So...

00:41:02.617 --> 00:41:06.283
We go after this damn thing...

00:41:06.317 --> 00:41:08.250
Together.

00:41:08.283 --> 00:41:10.517
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
